<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\{xy\in E(G)\colon|\psi(x)-\psi(y)|=3\}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\{xy\in E(G)\colon|\psi(x)-\psi(y)|=3\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">These three graphs edge-partition <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\cup U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\cup U</annotation></semantics></math> is bipartite under the labels modulo <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cup U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cup U</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-colourable under the labels modulo <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> be the sets of vertices with even and odd labels,
respectively.
Every component of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> lies in one of these two sets.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmclaimx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmclaimx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim</span></span><span id="Thmclaimx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmclaimx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmclaimx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmclaimx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The graph <math id="Thmclaimx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is connected.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_itemize">
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose otherwise, and let <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> be the vertex set of a component of <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is connected, at least one edge joins <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> to its complement.
Write each such edge as <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="xy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">xy</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in W</annotation></semantics></math>, and let</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{0}:=\{|\psi(x)-\psi(y)|\colon xy\in E(G),\ x\in W,\ y\notin W\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{0}:=\{|\psi(x)-\psi(y)|\colon xy\in E(G),\ x\in W,\ y\notin W\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">None of these edges belongs to <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\emptyset\neq D_{0}\subseteq\{2,3,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\emptyset\neq D_{0}\subseteq\{2,3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\in D_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\in D_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=-1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\notin D_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\notin D_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\in D_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\in D_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=2</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise, and let <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{0}^{r}=\{\ell+r\colon\ell\in D_{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{0}^{r}=\{\ell+r\colon\ell\in D_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In each case, <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\notin D_{0}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∉</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\notin D_{0}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{0}^{r}\cap\{1,5\}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{0}^{r}\cap\{1,5\}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus the new map remains proper, preserves every old <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>-edge, and gains a
new one, contradicting the choice of <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Put <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D:=\{a\in A\colon d_{O}(a)\text{ is odd}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is odd</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D:=\{a\in A\colon d_{O}(a)\text{ is odd}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Call a component <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[A]</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">bad</em> if <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(K)</annotation></semantics></math> is odd and <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(K)\subseteq D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(K)\subseteq D</annotation></semantics></math>.
In each bad <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, choose an edge <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> such that every component of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-f_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-f_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>
has an even number of edges: take a non-bridge if <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> contains a cycle, and a
leaf edge otherwise.
Choose an end <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and an edge <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{K}b_{K}\in E(O)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{K}b_{K}\in E(O)</annotation></semantics></math>, which exists
because <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{K}\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{K}\in D</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Group the chosen <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-edges by their endpoint in <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.
Put all of them in a graph <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and, for each group of odd size, also put
in <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> the edge <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> associated with one of the chosen <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-edges in that
group.
The subgraphs of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to distinct groups are vertex-disjoint:
vertices contributed in <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> by different choices of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> lie in different
components of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[A]</annotation></semantics></math>, and different groups have different centres in <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.
An even group is an even star.
An odd group is an odd star with one extra edge attached at a leaf; this is a
two-edge path when the group has size <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a larger odd group, the centre has odd degree at least <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, the extended
leaf has degree <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, and all other vertices have degree <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is locally irregular and every component of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> has an even number
of edges.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Put <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{\prime}:=O-E(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{\prime}:=O-E(P)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}:=T-E(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}:=T-E(P)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}:=\{a\in A\colon d_{O^{\prime}}(a)\text{ is odd}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is odd</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}:=\{a\in A\colon d_{O^{\prime}}(a)\text{ is odd}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> loses exactly one incident <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-edge, so <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{O^{\prime}}(v_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{O^{\prime}}(v_{K})</annotation></semantics></math> is even and
<math id="S3.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{K}\notin D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{K}\notin D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{K}\notin E(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{K}\notin E(P)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> remains a component of <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}[A]</annotation></semantics></math> with an odd
number of edges and contains <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{K}\notin D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{K}\notin D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{K}\in E(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{K}\in E(P)</annotation></semantics></math>, every component of <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-f_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-f_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> has an even number of edges.
Every other component of <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[A]</annotation></semantics></math> with an odd number of edges was not bad and
hence contained a vertex outside <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>; neither its edges nor the <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-degrees
of its vertices were changed.
Consequently, every component of <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}[A]</annotation></semantics></math> with an odd number of edges contains
a vertex outside <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since both <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(G)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(P)</annotation></semantics></math> are even, so is</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(U\cup T^{\prime}\cup O^{\prime})=e(G)-e(P)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(U\cup T^{\prime}\cup O^{\prime})=e(G)-e(P)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">In each component of <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with an odd number of edges, choose a vertex
outside <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Such a vertex exists by the previous paragraph for components contained
in <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, while every vertex of a component contained in <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> lies outside <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Apply part (i) of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2. Structural information by orientations ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> separately to the components
of <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, prescribing odd indegree at the chosen vertex of each component with
an odd number of edges and even indegree at every other vertex.
Denote the resulting orientation by <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{T}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{T}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is even for every <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choose a spanning tree <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> and orient the edges of <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U-E(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U-E(W)</annotation></semantics></math>
arbitrarily.
Define <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\colon V(G)\to\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\colon V(G)\to\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> by requiring</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(v)\equiv\begin{cases}1-d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(v),&amp;v\in D^{\prime},\\
-d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(v),&amp;v\notin D^{\prime}\end{cases}\pmod{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(v)\equiv\begin{cases}1-d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(v),&amp;v\in D^{\prime},\\
-d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(v),&amp;v\notin D^{\prime}\end{cases}\pmod{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is bipartite with parts <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D^{\prime}|\equiv\sum_{a\in A}d_{O^{\prime}}(a)=e(O^{\prime})\pmod{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≡</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D^{\prime}|\equiv\sum_{a\in A}d_{O^{\prime}}(a)=e(O^{\prime})\pmod{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Together with the evenness of <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(U\cup T^{\prime}\cup O^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(U\cup T^{\prime}\cup O^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, this gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v\in V(G)}\eta(v)\equiv|D^{\prime}|-\sum_{v\in V(G)}d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(v)=|D^{\prime}|-e(T^{\prime})\equiv e(U)\pmod{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v\in V(G)}\eta(v)\equiv|D^{\prime}|-\sum_{v\in V(G)}d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(v)=|D^{\prime}|-e(T^{\prime})\equiv e(U)\pmod{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Part (i) of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2. Structural information by orientations ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> therefore extends the chosen
orientation to an orientation <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{U}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{-}_{\vec{U}}(v)\equiv\eta(v)\pmod{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{-}_{\vec{U}}(v)\equiv\eta(v)\pmod{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for every vertex <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{-}_{\vec{U}}(v)+d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(v)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{-}_{\vec{U}}(v)+d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">is odd precisely when <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, if <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{-}_{\vec{T}^{\prime}}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is even, so <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{-}_{\vec{U}}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{-}_{\vec{U}}(a)</annotation></semantics></math>
is odd and therefore positive.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choose one edge of <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> directed into each vertex of <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>
be their set.
Every edge of <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> has exactly one endpoint in <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, so the chosen edges are
distinct and</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{S}(a)=\begin{cases}1,&amp;a\in D^{\prime},\\
0,&amp;a\in A\setminus D^{\prime}\,.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{S}(a)=\begin{cases}1,&amp;a\in D^{\prime},\\
0,&amp;a\in A\setminus D^{\prime}\,.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{\prime}\cup S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{\prime}\cup S</annotation></semantics></math> is bipartite and has even degree at every vertex of <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 3.1. ‣ 3.1. A general chromatic bound ‣ 3. Chromatic bounds ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> gives at most four colours.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be the orientation of <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R:=(U-S)\cup T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R:=(U-S)\cup T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> inherited from
<math id="S3.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{T}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{T}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
At each vertex of <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, deleting <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> removes exactly one incoming edge, while
no edge of <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> enters a vertex outside <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence every indegree in <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is even.
Summing the indegrees in each component shows that every component of <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> has
an even number of edges.
Since <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi(R)\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi(R)\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1. A general chromatic bound ‣ 3. Chromatic bounds ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> gives <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{\prime}_{\mathrm{irr}}(R)\leq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>χ</mi><mi>irr</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{\prime}_{\mathrm{irr}}(R)\leq 10</annotation></semantics></math>.
The edge-partition into <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{\prime}\cup S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>O</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{\prime}\cup S</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> now gives
<math id="S3.SS2.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{\prime}_{\mathrm{irr}}(G)\leq 1+4+10=15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>χ</mi><mi>irr</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{\prime}_{\mathrm{irr}}(G)\leq 1+4+10=15</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the second assertion, let <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be decomposable.
Every component of <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is then decomposable.
For each component having an odd number of edges, apply
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.1. A general chromatic bound ‣ 3. Chromatic bounds ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, and let <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> be the union of the locally irregular
subgraphs thereby obtained.
These subgraphs lie in distinct components of <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is locally
irregular and can be assigned at most one additional colour.
Components of <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> having an even number of edges are unchanged, and the lemma
ensures that every component left inside an originally odd component has an
even number of edges.
Thus every component of <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G-E(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G-E(L)</annotation></semantics></math> has an even number of edges.
Since <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G-E(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G-E(L)</annotation></semantics></math> is still <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>-colourable, the first assertion gives at
most <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math> further colours.
Hence <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{\prime}_{\mathrm{irr}}(G)\leq 1+15=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>χ</mi><mi>irr</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{\prime}_{\mathrm{irr}}(G)\leq 1+15=16</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Preserving connectivity</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1. </span>Selections</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a graph <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(H)</annotation></semantics></math> denote its number of components, including isolated
vertices.
For a connected graph <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq E(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq E(H)</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{H}(A):=|A|-c(H-A)+1\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{H}(A):=|A|-c(H-A)+1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This is the maximum number of edges of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> that can be deleted while preserving
connectivity.
Indeed, contract the components of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H-A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H-A</annotation></semantics></math>.
The resulting connected multigraph has <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(H-A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(H-A)</annotation></semantics></math> vertices, so at least
<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(H-A)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(H-A)-1</annotation></semantics></math> edges of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> must be retained.
Conversely, retaining the edges corresponding to a spanning tree of this
multigraph and deleting all other edges of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> attains this bound.
The maximum-deletion interpretation also shows that <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is monotone.
In addition,</p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{H}(A)+\mu_{H}(B)\geq\mu_{H}(A\cup B)+\mu_{H}(A\cap B)\qquad\text{for all }A,B\subseteq E(H)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{H}(A)+\mu_{H}(B)\geq\mu_{H}(A\cup B)+\mu_{H}(A\cap B)\qquad\text{for all }A,B\subseteq E(H)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Indeed, put <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X:=H-A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X:=H-A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y:=H-B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y:=H-B</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n:=|V(H)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n:=|V(H)|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Extend a spanning forest <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\cap Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\cap Y</annotation></semantics></math> to spanning forests <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.
The graph <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{X}\cup F_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{X}\cup F_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> has the same components as <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\cup Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\cup Y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}\subseteq F_{X}\cap F_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}\subseteq F_{X}\cap F_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-c(X\cup Y)\leq e(F_{X}\cup F_{Y})\leq e(F_{X})+e(F_{Y})-e(F_{0})=n-c(X)-c(Y)+c(X\cap Y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-c(X\cup Y)\leq e(F_{X}\cup F_{Y})\leq e(F_{X})+e(F_{Y})-e(F_{0})=n-c(X)-c(Y)+c(X\cap Y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(X)+c(Y)\leq c(X\cap Y)+c(X\cup Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(X)+c(Y)\leq c(X\cap Y)+c(X\cup Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\cap Y=H-(A\cup B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\cap Y=H-(A\cup B)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\cup Y=H-(A\cap B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\cup Y=H-(A\cap B)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A|+|B|=|A\cup B|+|A\cap B|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A|+|B|=|A\cup B|+|A\cap B|</annotation></semantics></math>, the inequality in (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 4.1. Selections ‣ 4. Preserving connectivity ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)
follows from (<a href="#S4.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 4.1. Selections ‣ 4. Preserving connectivity ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be connected, and let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{i})_{i\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{i})_{i\in I}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite family of subsets
of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(H)</annotation></semantics></math>.
There are distinct edges <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}\in A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}\in A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H-\{e_{i}\colon i\in I\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H-\{e_{i}\colon i\in I\}</annotation></semantics></math> is connected if and only if</span></p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{H}\left(\bigcup_{i\in J}A_{i}\right)\geq|J|\qquad\text{for every }J\subseteq I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for every </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{H}\left(\bigcup_{i\in J}A_{i}\right)\geq|J|\qquad\text{for every }J\subseteq I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose first that distinct edges <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}\in A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}\in A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be chosen and that their
simultaneous deletion leaves <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> connected.
For every <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\subseteq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\subseteq I</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|J|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|J|</annotation></semantics></math> edges in <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e_{i}\colon i\in J\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e_{i}\colon i\in J\}</annotation></semantics></math> belong
to <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{i\in J}A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{i\in J}A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and may also be deleted while preserving
connectivity.
The interpretation of <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> above gives (<a href="#S4.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4.1. Selections ‣ 4. Preserving connectivity ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Conversely, shrink the sets <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, one edge at a time, while
preserving (<a href="#S4.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4.1. Selections ‣ 4. Preserving connectivity ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).
Suppose that, in the resulting inclusion-minimal family, some <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> contains
distinct edges <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Write <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(J):=\bigcup_{j\in J}A_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(J):=\bigcup_{j\in J}A_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Removing <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> violates the condition, and the violating index set
must contain <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence there is <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{x}\subseteq I\setminus\{k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{x}\subseteq I\setminus\{k\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for
<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P:=(A_{k}\setminus\{x\})\cup A(J_{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P:=(A_{k}\setminus\{x\})\cup A(J_{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{H}(P)&lt;|J_{x}|+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{H}(P)&lt;|J_{x}|+1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is integer-valued, <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{H}(P)\leq|J_{x}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{H}(P)\leq|J_{x}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly, there is <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{y}\subseteq I\setminus\{k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{y}\subseteq I\setminus\{k\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q:=(A_{k}\setminus\{y\})\cup A(J_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q:=(A_{k}\setminus\{y\})\cup A(J_{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{H}(Q)\leq|J_{y}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{H}(Q)\leq|J_{y}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\cup Q=A_{k}\cup A(J_{x}\cup J_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\cup Q=A_{k}\cup A(J_{x}\cup J_{y})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\cap Q\supseteq A(J_{x}\cap J_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>⊇</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\cap Q\supseteq A(J_{x}\cap J_{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The selection condition and monotonicity give</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{H}(P\cup Q)\geq|J_{x}\cup J_{y}|+1,\qquad\mu_{H}(P\cap Q)\geq|J_{x}\cap J_{y}|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{H}(P\cup Q)\geq|J_{x}\cup J_{y}|+1,\qquad\mu_{H}(P\cap Q)\geq|J_{x}\cap J_{y}|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ 4.1. Selections ‣ 4. Preserving connectivity ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|J_{x}|+|J_{y}|\geq\mu_{H}(P)+\mu_{H}(Q)\geq|J_{x}\cup J_{y}|+1+|J_{x}\cap J_{y}|=|J_{x}|+|J_{y}|+1\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|J_{x}|+|J_{y}|\geq\mu_{H}(P)+\mu_{H}(Q)\geq|J_{x}\cup J_{y}|+1+|J_{x}\cap J_{y}|=|J_{x}|+|J_{y}|+1\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">a contradiction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus every <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a singleton, say <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}=\{e_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}=\{e_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying (<a href="#S4.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4.1. Selections ‣ 4. Preserving connectivity ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) to <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> and using the interpretation
of <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|I|\leq\mu_{H}\bigl(\{e_{i}\colon i\in I\}\bigr)\leq|\{e_{i}\colon i\in I\}|\leq|I|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|I|\leq\mu_{H}\bigl(\{e_{i}\colon i\in I\}\bigr)\leq|\{e_{i}\colon i\in I\}|\leq|I|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Equality throughout shows that the edges <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct and that all of
them can be deleted while preserving connectivity.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>Selecting crossing edges while preserving connectivity</h3>

<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be a connected graph, let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> be a
crossing-optimal <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-labelling of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be its crossing graph.
Then <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is connected.
Moreover, if <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv</annotation></semantics></math> is monochromatic with <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(u)=\varphi(v)=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(u)=\varphi(v)=i</annotation></semantics></math>, then,
for every label <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>, the vertices <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> belong to the same
component of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C[\varphi^{-1}(\{i,j\})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C[\varphi^{-1}(\{i,j\})]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv</annotation></semantics></math> be monochromatic with label <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> be the
vertex set of the component of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C[\varphi^{-1}(\{i,j\})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C[\varphi^{-1}(\{i,j\})]</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin W</annotation></semantics></math>, interchange labels <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>.
The edge <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv</annotation></semantics></math> becomes crossing, and no crossing edge is lost: a crossing edge
with exactly one end in <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> has its other end labelled outside <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{i,j\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{i,j\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This contradicts crossing-optimality and proves the second assertion.
In particular, the ends of every monochromatic edge belong to the same
component of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is connected, so is <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
