<div id="S4.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, and put <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=\bigcup_{(a,j)\in\mathcal{X}}L(a,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=\bigcup_{(a,j)\in\mathcal{X}}L(a,j)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,v)\in E(\vec{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,v)\in E(\vec{F})</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4.2. Selecting crossing edges while preserving connectivity ‣ 4. Preserving connectivity ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> gives a path from <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>
to <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C[\varphi^{-1}(B(\varphi(v)))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C[\varphi^{-1}(B(\varphi(v)))]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Every edge of <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> has endpoint labels in two different sets
among <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1},B_{2},B_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1},B_{2},B_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas this path uses labels from only one of them.
Thus the path lies in <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C-A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C-A</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of components of <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C-A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C-A</annotation></semantics></math>.
Contract them, discard loops, and choose a spanning tree <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> of the
resulting connected multigraph, identifying its edges with their preimages
in <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.
Put <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D:=A\setminus E(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D:=A\setminus E(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C-D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C-D</annotation></semantics></math> is connected and, by (<a href="#S4.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 4.1. Selections ‣ 4. Preserving connectivity ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D|=\mu_{C}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D|=\mu_{C}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a pair <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> of labels lying in two distinct sets among <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1},B_{2},B_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1},B_{2},B_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
identify its two labels with the elements of <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> consist of the pairs <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,j)\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,j)\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S4.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\varphi(v),j\}=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\varphi(v),j\}=p</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> consist of the edges
of <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> whose end labels form <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of heads occurring in <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose the variables <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\xi_{v})_{v\in\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\xi_{v})_{v\in\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> independently and uniformly
from <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and put <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{v}:=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{v}:=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choose a root <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}\in\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}\in\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{K_{0}}:=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{K_{0}}:=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For an edge <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="KK^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">KK^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> directed away from the root, represented by <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="xy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">xy</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, define recursively</span></p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{K^{\prime}}-\sigma_{K}\equiv\xi_{x}-\xi_{y}\pmod{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{K^{\prime}}-\sigma_{K}\equiv\xi_{x}-\xi_{y}\pmod{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">These shifts are homogeneous linear forms in the variables <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For every <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and every vertex <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in K</annotation></semantics></math> whose label lies
in <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, interchange the two labels of <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> precisely when <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{v}+\sigma_{K}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{v}+\sigma_{K}=1</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Leave all other labels unchanged.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">A crossing edge can be lost only if its original labels form <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C-D=(C-A)\cup E(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C-D=(C-A)\cup E(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, first suppose that such an edge lies
in <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C-A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C-A</annotation></semantics></math>.
Neither end belongs to <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, since otherwise the edge would lie
in <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, and both ends receive the same component shift.
If instead it belongs to <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, the total shifts at its ends agree
by (<a href="#S4.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.2. Selecting crossing edges while preserving connectivity ‣ 4. Preserving connectivity ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>).
Thus every edge of <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C-D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C-D</annotation></semantics></math> remains crossing.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,j)\in\mathcal{X}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,j)\in\mathcal{X}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The ends have the same original label and lie in the same component of <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C-A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C-A</annotation></semantics></math>,
so their component shifts cancel.
Here <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{u}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{u}=0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.
Thus <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{v}-\xi_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{v}-\xi_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniform on <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the edge <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv</annotation></semantics></math> becomes
crossing with probability <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each arc occurs at most once in <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the expected gain is at
least <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{X}_{p}|/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{X}_{p}|/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Only edges of <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> can be lost.
For each such edge, the final binary difference of its labels is <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> plus a
homogeneous linear form in independent bits.
If the form is zero, this difference never vanishes; if it is nonzero, it is
uniform on <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus the edge is lost with probability at most <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
By crossing-optimality and linearity of expectation,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\geq\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{\mathrm{cr}}]\geq\frac{|\mathcal{X}_{p}|-|D_{p}|}{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>cr</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\geq\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{\mathrm{cr}}]\geq\frac{|\mathcal{X}_{p}|-|D_{p}|}{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{cr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>cr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{cr}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the change in the number of crossing edges.
As <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> ranges over all pairs of labels lying in two distinct sets
among <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1},B_{2},B_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1},B_{2},B_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sets <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> partition <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and the
sets <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> partition <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.
Summing <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{X}_{p}|\leq|D_{p}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{X}_{p}|\leq|D_{p}|</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{X}|\leq|D|=\mu_{C}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{X}|\leq|D|=\mu_{C}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There are distinct edges <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{a,j}\in L(a,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{a,j}\in L(a,j)</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,j)\in\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,j)\in\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math>,
whose simultaneous deletion leaves <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> connected.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4.1. Selections ‣ 4. Preserving connectivity ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> to the lists <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(a,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(a,j)</annotation></semantics></math>, using
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4.2. Selecting crossing edges while preserving connectivity ‣ 4. Preserving connectivity ‣ An 18-colour bound for locally irregular decompositions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
